## 🧠 Key Takeaways

- Every device in a network needs a **unique IP address**
- IP operates at the **Network Layer (Layer 3)** of the OSI model
- IPv4 addresses are **32-bit numeric values**, typically written in dotted decimal format
- IP is **connectionless**, meaning it doesn’t guarantee delivery
- Routers use IP addresses to **forward packets between networks**

